WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.367 --> 00:00:03.601
-Guys, it is time
for that beloved tradition.

00:00:03.601 --> 00:00:07.000
-"Is there a 'Stache
Under That Mask?"

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:08.601
-Here we go.
That's right.

00:00:08.601 --> 00:00:10.701
♪♪

00:00:10.701 --> 00:00:13.267
That's right.
This is a game where we --

00:00:13.267 --> 00:00:15.667
This is a game where
we pick a random audience member

00:00:15.667 --> 00:00:18.734
and guess if there's a 'stache
under their mask.

00:00:18.734 --> 00:00:21.033
So, please welcome
tonight's audience member,

00:00:21.033 --> 00:00:22.434
Michael Christian.

00:00:22.434 --> 00:00:23.834
Michael, where are you sitting?
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:23.834 --> 00:00:25.567
Alright.
Michael, come on down.

00:00:25.567 --> 00:00:28.934
♪♪

00:00:28.934 --> 00:00:30.367
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:30.367 --> 00:00:32.501
♪♪

00:00:32.501 --> 00:00:34.868
Welcome, buddy.
Please have a seat.

00:00:34.868 --> 00:00:36.200
How are you?
-Hi.

00:00:36.200 --> 00:00:37.634
-Nice to see you.
-Nice to see you.

00:00:37.634 --> 00:00:39.100
-Welcome, welcome, welcome.

00:00:39.100 --> 00:00:41.601
Welcome to the game "Is There
a 'Stache Under That Mask?"

00:00:41.601 --> 00:00:43.667
Michael, where you from?

00:00:43.667 --> 00:00:45.868
-I'm from Orlando, Florida.
-Orlando, Florida.

00:00:45.868 --> 00:00:47.501
[ Cheers and applause ]
Alright, very good.

00:00:47.501 --> 00:00:49.234
That's all --
That's all I can ask you.

00:00:49.234 --> 00:00:50.767
-[ Laughs ]
-That's all I can ask you.

00:00:50.767 --> 00:00:51.901
Alright,
now we have to figure out

00:00:51.901 --> 00:00:54.400
if you've got a 'stache
under that mask.

00:00:54.400 --> 00:00:56.601
Quest,
since you're the furthest away,

00:00:56.601 --> 00:00:57.767
what do you think?

00:00:57.767 --> 00:00:59.234
You can ask him one question
if you want,

00:00:59.234 --> 00:01:01.000
and then you must make
your guess.

00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:02.501
-Alright.
-Or, if you think you know,

00:01:02.501 --> 00:01:03.567
you don't have to ask
a question.

00:01:03.567 --> 00:01:05.734
-I'm going to ask a question.
-Okay.

00:01:05.734 --> 00:01:08.267
-At Starbucks...

00:01:08.267 --> 00:01:12.300
would you order hot chocolate
with or without whipped cream?

00:01:12.300 --> 00:01:13.601
[ Laughter ]
-Oh.

00:01:13.601 --> 00:01:15.701
[ Audience ohs ]

00:01:15.701 --> 00:01:17.334
-I don't go to Starbucks,

00:01:17.334 --> 00:01:19.634
but if I ordered
a hot chocolate,

00:01:19.634 --> 00:01:21.400
I would get it
with whipped cream.

00:01:21.400 --> 00:01:23.567
-Oh.
-Oh.

00:01:23.567 --> 00:01:25.000
-What's your guess?

00:01:25.000 --> 00:01:26.200
-I think he's trying
to throw me off.

00:01:26.200 --> 00:01:27.734
I think he has a 'stache.

00:01:27.734 --> 00:01:29.801
-[ Laughs ] That's ridiculous.

00:01:29.801 --> 00:01:32.067
You asked -- Alright.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:32.067 --> 00:01:34.000
[ Laughs ]

00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:35.701
Trying to throw you off.

00:01:35.701 --> 00:01:37.000
-I don't trust anything now.

00:01:37.000 --> 00:01:38.968
-Yeah, Higgins --
Higgins, your turn.

00:01:38.968 --> 00:01:41.100
What is -- What is your guess,
or do you have a question?

00:01:41.100 --> 00:01:42.234
-I have one question.

00:01:42.234 --> 00:01:44.000
-Alright.
You can ask one question.

00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:45.367
-Do you have a mustache?

00:01:45.367 --> 00:01:46.834
-No, Higgins, you -- No.
[ Rim shot ]

00:01:46.834 --> 00:01:49.501
It's got to be -- You can't ask
the -- an obvious question.

00:01:49.501 --> 00:01:50.968
-Okay. Alright.
-A different question.

00:01:50.968 --> 00:01:53.901
